safe.desc = The game can be saved any time. However, as in the case of SCP Objects, a Safe classification does not mean that handling it does not pose a threat.
euclid = Euclid
euclid.desc = In Euclid difficulty, saving is only allowed at specific locations marked by lit up computer screens. Euclid-class objects are inherently unpredictable, so that reliable containment is not always possible.
keter = Keter
keter.desc = Keter-class objects are considered the most dangerous ones in Foundation containment. The same can be said for this difficulty level: the SCPs are more aggressive, and you have only one life - when you die, the game is over.
