; --- 035 ---

[SFX\SCP\035\RadioHelp1.ogg]
voice=scientist
italic=true
0.7=Hello? Please, can anyone hear me?
4.9=Anyone? I need help, and medical attention too! Please!
12.2=<length=5.5>I'm currently in the Heavy Containment Zone beyond Checkpoint E, and I'm locked in SCP-035's containment chamber.

[SFX\SCP\035\RadioHelp2.ogg]
0.6=<voice=scientist,italic=true,length=6>Please! I know my way around this compound. If you can get me out of here, I'll help you out of the facility and into the surface!

[SFX\SCP\035\Help1.ogg]
voice=scientist
0.57=Oh thank god!
2.48=Someone actually found me! I thought I was done for a moment there, haha!

[SFX\SCP\035\Help2.ogg]
0.2=<voice=scientist>I can get us both safely to the surface. Just find the control panel in there and open the chamber doors for me.

[SFX\SCP\035\Idle1.ogg]
0.19=<voice=scientist>Well? What are you waiting for?

[SFX\SCP\035\Idle2.ogg]
voice=scientist
0=What? Do you not-
1.78=<length=6.6>Alright, I admit it, I wouldn't blame you if you don't think I look trustworthy. But, please! I need your help and quickly!
9.0=<length=5.5>The mask has been stuck to my face for some time now and I think I might need medical attention or it might kill me from the inside.
15.0=Just let me out so I can find us an exit in a matter of time.

[SFX\SCP\035\Idle3.ogg]
voice=scientist
0=<caption=true>*sigh*
1.75=I'm starting to lose my patience here.

[SFX\SCP\035\Idle4.ogg]
0.3=<voice=scientist>What are you doing just standing there?

[SFX\SCP\035\Idle5.ogg]
voice=scientist
0.7=You know... the Mobile Task Force will be entering the facility any minute now. 
5.4=Guess what they do to stray Class Ds like you?

[SFX\SCP\035\Idle6.ogg]
0.95=<voice=scientist>Fine. Good luck getting out all on your own.

[SFX\SCP\035\Idle7.ogg]
0.5=<voice=scientist>Are you even listening?

[SFX\SCP\035\Closet1.ogg]
voice=scientist
0.64=Alright, look. 
2.24=<length=9>If you still don't think I'm trustworthy enough, there's a locked storage room behind you. You probably noticed that it's guarded with a 4 digit passcode.
9.7=Inside is some useful equipment. As well as a pill of SCP-500. 
14.9=The passcode is 5-7-3-1. Got it?
19.7=5-7-3-1.

[SFX\SCP\035\Closet2.ogg]
0.43=<voice=scientist>You see? You can trust me. Now please, just hurry and open the door!

[SFX\SCP\035\Escape.ogg]
voice=scientist
0=Unfortunately, I never had any intentions of taking you with me. So this is where we part ways. 
6.0=But for the sake of my freedom...
8.7=<length=7>I have reason to believe that SCP-079 has taken control of the facility's systems, including the door system.
15.8=<length=7.5>Your best bet is to appeal to it somehow. Hopefully you can come to a compromise. However, it does not control the warheads.
23.8=Which you should disable remotely in the event that something goes wrong.

[SFX\SCP\035\Gased1.ogg]
voice=scientist
0=Wait, what the hell are you doing? What the hell are-
2.95=<caption=true>*choking*
4.2=What are you-
5.0=Please- Why-
6.28=Just please-
8.0=I can't breathe!
10.45=No!
11.9=<caption=true>*coughing*

[SFX\SCP\035\Gased2.ogg]
0=<voice=scientist,caption=true,length=15>*choking*

[SFX\SCP\035\GasedStop1.ogg]
voice=scientist
0=<caption=true>*coughing*
2.5=Thank you!
5.85=Just please...
7.95=Don't do that again...

[SFX\SCP\035\GasedStop2.ogg]
voice=scientist
0=<caption=true>*coughing*
2.0=<caption=true>*sigh*
3.85=Now...
5.25=Was that really necessary?
7.5=I offer you some help and you try to thank me by suffocating me?

[SFX\SCP\035\GasedCloset.ogg]
voice=scientist
0.25=Now, now... I think we got off on the wrong foot here. Really.
4.77=To prove that I'm not up to no good, try that locked door over there. The code is 5-7-3-1.
10.95=5-7-3-1! Got it?
13.80=You'll find all sorts of goodies in there, okay? Please, just not the gas again.

[SFX\SCP\035\GasedEscape.ogg]
voice=scientist
0.39=Unfortunately, I can't take you with me.
3.35=You're too much of a liability in many ways. So yes, I did lie to you.
8.5=But for the sake of my freedom...
10.55=The easiest way to get out safely is probably Gate A.
15.25=<length=7.5>The security is pretty high, but if you manage to sneak past the guards and reach the lower level under the bridge, there's an unguarded service tunnel.
23.35=That's your way out.

[SFX\SCP\035\GasedKilled1.ogg]
voice=scientist
2.18=So, you really don't wanna leave this place alive, do you?
6.97=<length=8>You know, there's no way a lone D Class like you will make it to the surface safely. Even if you did, they'd gun you down the moment you came across their reticles.

[SFX\SCP\035\GasedKilled2.ogg]
voice=scientist
0.23=I'll give you one more chance here. 
2.6=Just, open the chambers doors and we'll forget about this little gas incident.

[SFX\SCP\035\KilledEscape.ogg]
voice=scientist
0.5=I commemorate you for your help, but I have no further business with you.
4.9=I have no intentions of taking a person who earned their imprisonment with me.
10.6=But for the sake of my freedom...
12.7=<length=5.5>The simplest way for you to get out safely is to go and find SCP-012 in the Light Containment Zone.
19.0=If you can read between the lines...
21.7=...it'll be as interpretable as a map.
24.3=Good luck.

; --- 049 ---

[SFX\SCP\049\Searching1.ogg]
0=<voice=049>I know you're in here.

[SFX\SCP\049\Searching2.ogg]
0=<voice=049>There's no need to hide, I'm here to help.

[SFX\SCP\049\Searching3.ogg]
0=<voice=049>I hear you breathing.

[SFX\SCP\049\Searching4.ogg]
0=<voice=049>I can see you're not well. The sickness has taken hold of you.

[SFX\SCP\049\Searching5.ogg]
0=<voice=049>Fear not, I'm not trying to harm you.

[SFX\SCP\049\Searching6.ogg]
0=<voice=049>I sense the disease in you.

[SFX\SCP\049\Searching7.ogg]
0=<voice=049,length=12>Ring-a-ring o' roses, a pocket full of posies. A-tishoo, a-tishoo. We all fall down.

[SFX\SCP\049\Spotted1.ogg]
0=<voice=049>Oh my, yet another victim of the disease.

[SFX\SCP\049\Spotted2.ogg]
0=<voice=049>You are not a doctor.

[SFX\SCP\049\Spotted3.ogg]
0=<voice=049>I am the cure.

[SFX\SCP\049\Spotted4.ogg]
0=<voice=049>Do not be afraid, I am the cure.

[SFX\SCP\049\Spotted5.ogg]
0=<voice=049>There you are.

[SFX\SCP\049\Spotted6.ogg]
0=<voice=049>Hello.

[SFX\SCP\049\Spotted7.ogg]
0=<voice=049>Greetings.

[SFX\SCP\049\DetectedInChamber.ogg]
0=<voice=049>Ah, I wasn't aware we had company.
3.4=<voice=049>We rarely get visitors down here.

[SFX\SCP\049\Kidnap1.ogg]
0=<voice=049>It will hurt less if you lie still.

[SFX\SCP\049\Kidnap2.ogg]
0=<voice=049>I can assure you, my cure is most effective.

[SFX\SCP\049\714Equipped.ogg]
0=<voice=049>Stop resisting! I'm here to cure you.

[SFX\SCP\049\TakeOffHazmat.ogg]
0=<voice=049>Let's get this strange garment out of the way.

[SFX\SCP\049\Room2SL1.ogg]
0=<voice=049,length=9>Good heavens! It's worse than I thought. Like wildfire, it spreads. They should've brought me here sooner.

[SFX\SCP\049\Room2SL2.ogg]
0=<voice=049,length=5.5>I need to get to work before the disease consumes the rest of these poor souls.

