[SFX\Radio\RadioAlarm2.ogg]
0.62=<r=128,g=128,b=128,italic=true>This site is experiencing multiple Keter and Euclid-level containment breaches. Full-site lockdown initiated.

[SFX\Radio\scpradio1.ogg]
4.0=<voice=radio,length=7>You're listening to SCP Foundation on-site radio! Your 24/7 source for pre-recorded messages.

[SFX\Radio\scpradio2.ogg]
voice=radio
3.2=<length=7>A reminder, in the event of an XK-Class end-of-the-world scenario, don't panic. It won't help.
11.3=Nothing at all will help.
13.5=However, panicking will help probably the least.

[SFX\Radio\scpradio3.ogg]
voice=radio
2.9=Report all suspect behavior to your supervisors immediately.
7.64=If you haven't noticed any unusual activity recently, you're not looking hard enough.
12.7=A threat to security can originate from anywhere, and no one is above suspicion. Not even you.
18.92=Stay paranoid. Stay vigilant.

[SFX\Radio\scpradio4.ogg]
voice=radio
3.5=Should you hear a different voice announcing for SCP Foundation on-site radio, disregard it entirely.
9.45=He is not a foundation employee!
11.8=<length=8>He is trying to trick you and cannot be trusted. Any advice he gives can only inevitably lead to destruction, death, and utter chaos.
20.95=You are immeasurably better off listening to me.

[SFX\Radio\scpradio5.ogg]
voice=radio
3.8=<length=8>In the extremely unlikely event of a catastrophic power failure and subsequent facility-wide containment breach, just remember the crisis ABCs.
12.6=<length=8>A for armaments. B for blinking, come the lack of. And C for cardiovascular fortitude.
21.5=<length=7>As they say, shoot, stare, and sprint! Or, feed the oncoming monster one of your friends.
29.3=Stay alive. Stay vigilant.

[SFX\Radio\scpradio6.ogg]
voice=radio
0=<caption=true,voice=default>[From Radio, Ghostly Exhale]
3.2=<caption=true,voice=default,length=10>[From Radio, Distorted Music]
10.10=Every single thing he says is a lie.
14.7=Every single one.
19.6=Don't listen to him.
24.0=You can trust me.
29.65=I can get you out of this.
33.75=I can get you away from all of this.
40.40=Just listen to me.

[SFX\Radio\scpradio7.ogg]
voice=radio
2.6=<length=7>Don't forget, Wednesday is pizza day! So head on down to the cafeteria and grab yourself a hot slice! 
11.7=<bold=true>(The SCP Foundation holds no liability for any injuries or illnesses sustained or contracted through the attendance of pizza day.)

[SFX\Radio\scpradio8.ogg]
voice=radio
3.2=When dining in the facility cafeteria, always remember to check your rations for the deadly seven.
8.6=<length=9>Strychnine, Arsenic Trioxide, Nitrobenzene, Mercury, Epichlorohydrin, Acetone Thiosemicarbazone, and spiders.
17.58=Stay healthy! Stay vigilant.

; --- ENDINGS ---

; --- GATE A ---

[SFX\Ending\GateA\Franklin.ogg]
0=<voice=franklin,length=10>SCP-106 has broken out of the facility at Gate A! Fire the H.I.D Turret immediately! Do not let it across the bridge!

[SFX\Ending\GateA\STOPRIGHTTHERE.ogg]
0.25=<voice=ntf>Stop right there!
3.75=<voice=ntf2>Class D has been found.

[SFX\Ending\GateA\CI.ogg]
0=<voice=ci>You know too much to let them get you. You're coming with us.

[SFX\Ending\GateA\EndingA1.ogg]
0.75=<voice=ntf>Sir, we're having a major problem here!
5.0=<voice=scientist>Please elaborate. Has the target been captured yet?
9.75=<voice=ntf>I'm not sure what's happening here. We entered the old service tunnel and it sort of...
14.35=<voice=ntf>...closed up on us.
16.2=<voice=ntf>Now we're trapped inside. Sanders is dead. Target's been lost.
22.2=<voice=scientist>Are you saying that the tunnel collapsed on you?
25.9=<voice=ntf>No. It didn't collapse. It seemed like an anomalous event.
31.4=<voice=ntf>Come and see for yourself, and send someone to get us out of here!

[SFX\Ending\GateA\EndingA2.ogg]
voice=scientist
2.1=<length=5.5>Testing Log [REDACTED]. Subject [REDACTED].
7.8=<length=11>Subject demonstrates extraordinary luck and complete mastery of even the most fatal of circumstances and an uncanny ability to predict even the most unpredictable of hazards.
18.9=Almost as if it has performed these impossible tasks several times before.
24.4=<length=5.7>Further testing is required to determine whether the subject should receive SCP classification.

; --- GATE B ---

[SFX\Ending\GateB\682Battle.ogg]
caption=true
0.5=[Explosions!]
5.65=<voice=pa,length=8,caption=false>SCP-682 just broke out at Gate B. I want all available helicopters and MTF units at Gate B now!
8.9=[Gunfire!]
10.4=[Explosions!]
13.3=[Gunfire!]
13.8=<voice=pa,length=8,caption=false>I repeat, SCP-682 is out of the facility! All available helicopters and MTF units to Gate B now!
16.4=[SCP-682 Roars!]
18.1=[Gunfire!]
20.5=[Large Explosion!]
23.1=<length=10>[Gunfire!]
25.5=[SCP-682 Growls]
35.0=[SCP-682 Growls]
37.5=[SCP-682 Roars!]
39.35=[Large Explosion!]

[SFX\Ending\GateB\DetonatingAlphaWarheads.ogg]
0.42=<voice=pa,length=10>We're detonating the Alpha warheads in T-minus 90 seconds! All personnel are advised to board the nearest helicopter or enter the nearest blast shelter immediately.

[SFX\Ending\GateB\AlphaWarheadsFail.ogg]
0.38=<voice=pa,length=12>We were unable to detonate the warheads for unknown reasons. All helicopters and MTF units go back to Gate B immediately. Capturing SCP-682 is now our number one priority.

[SFX\Ending\GateB\PlayerDetect.ogg]
0=<voice=ntf>There he is! Start shooting!

[SFX\Ending\GateB\EndingB1.ogg]
0=<voice=ntf>Sir, there's a Class D outside the elevator to Gate B. Should we send someone in to get him?
6.1=<voice=scientist>He might have some useful information about what's going on in there. I'll call-
11.15=<voice=ntf>Nevermind, sir. It looks like 173 already took care of him.

[SFX\Ending\GateB\EndingB2.ogg]
0.35=This is CH-1 to OH-6, have you located the target? Over.
6.25=OH-6 to CH-1, no sign of the target. I think we should send an MTF
15.25=CH-1 to OH-6, do you copy?

[SFX\Ending\GateB\EndingB3.ogg]
0.5=<voice=ntf,length=7>Sir, we found a dead Class D on the walkway outside Gate B. He's got multiple gunshot wounds in his chest.
7.75=<voice=ntf>I'd assume he was shot when we were fighting SCP-682.
11.8=<voice=scientist>I'd like to know how the hell did a Class D get past the gate.
16.3=<voice=scientist,length=8>Deliver me the security tapes from all the cameras near the gate and find out who was stationed there, before and during 682's escape attempt. 
26.10=<voice=ntf>Roger that, sir.

